Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::sq_push_stays_in_bounds`.

The defect: `SubmissionQueue::push` advances the tail with a bare `+ 1`, losing the `% entries`. The tail
doorbell is then written with a value equal to the ring depth, one past the last legal tail.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(sq.tail() < entries)`.

diff --git a/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/lib.rs b/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/lib.rs
index 7827ea4e1..093393f7e 100644
--- a/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/lib.rs
@@ -460,3 +460,3 @@ impl SubmissionQueue {
     pub fn push(&mut self) -> u16 {
-        let next = (self.tail + 1) % self.entries;
+        let next = self.tail + 1;
         assert!(next != self.head, "submission ring full");
